      "writtenOn": "2023-05-26T22:38:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think this needs to mention multiple files. If a client needs to write a single file atomically, which I expect to be a common case, then it can pass true here and commit after writing one file. If we allow the session object to be re-used though, which is needed to keep files open across transactions, it might be better to annotate the atomic regions with a separate method call.\n\nNote that this is an inefficient ipc interface though, passing flags at the ipc interface layer allows round-trips to be eliminated. The read/write api you have defined here can\u0027t necessarily be supported by the server since the idl will require the entire operation to be staged in memory, the api here seems more like a preview of to what we expect the wrapper library to provide, not the actual server/idl api.",
      "revId": "7d4afe914f0adf20e16033cc84953e6771744dd1",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
