      "writtenOn": "2023-05-30T18:00:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Couple things I don\u0027t understand here:\n\n1. Does it make sense for a client to _non_-atomically write to one file? If I change this to `boolean atomicCommits`, seem like we\u0027re implying that does make sense. It also means that impls that don\u0027t support session with multi-file atomic commits will have to return `UNSUPPORTED` from `IFile::Write`; I think it\u0027s better if we can error out earlier, ideally when the session is created asking for that functionality.\n\n2. Is there ipc inefficiency here that wasn\u0027t already there in `IFile` or `IDir`? I definitely agree that this is more round-trips that are strictly necessary, but thought we decided that was okay. I don\u0027t see why this api requires the operation to be staged in memory; can\u0027t the server write to temp files and move them on commit?",
      "parentUuid": "7af06663_e0380f1f",
      "revId": "7d4afe914f0adf20e16033cc84953e6771744dd1",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
